<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kwidzyn</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marienwerder</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kwidzyn, German Marienwerder, is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> near the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> founded a castle there in 1233 during its conquest of Pomesania, and it became the seat of the cathedral chapter of the Bishopric of Pomesania, whose brick Gothic castle and cathedral of the 14th century still stand. It remained German until 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kwidzyn.jpg" alt="Kwidzyn" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karina Pietuszyńska · CC BY-SA 3.0 pl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Budynek_Urz%C4%99du_Miejskiego_i_Rejonowego_w_Kwidzynie.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
